    "description": "A feature, a native function, native class, or native constant, is called native, built-in, native PHP, or internal, when it is part of the standard installation of PHP. For example, ``.``, dot operator for concatenation, or the ``stdClass`` class are native to PHP.\n\nOn the other hand, a feature is custom: that is, when defined by the developer or a PHP extension.",
